WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.129
Ghislaine Maxwell: convicted June 2021 on five federal counts.

00:00:05.079 --> 00:00:08.534
Sentenced to twenty years in June 2022.

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:13.931
Jeffrey Epstein: died in federal custody on August 10th, 2019.

00:00:13.931 --> 00:00:17.522
Ruled suicide by the New York City Medical Examiner.

00:00:17.522 --> 00:00:25.977
Three point five million pages released by the Department of Justice on January 30th, 2026, under the Epstein Files Transparency Act.

00:00:25.977 --> 00:00:28.784
Peter Nygard — the Canadian parallel.

00:00:28.784 --> 00:00:32.999
Convicted September 2024 on four sexual assault counts.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:35.295
Sentenced to eleven years.

00:00:35.295 --> 00:00:41.829
Nygard made documented Liberal Party donations and received a key to the City of Winnipeg in 2008.

00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:47.772
The connection between political access and institutional protection is not unique to the United States.

00:00:47.772 --> 00:00:54.034
In 2008, Alex Acosta negotiated a plea deal that shielded Epstein from federal prosecution.

00:00:54.034 --> 00:00:56.579
Thirty victims were not notified.

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:01.420
Palm Beach police investigated in 2005 and 2006.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:07.215
The investigation was transferred to the FBI — then closed via a non-prosecution agreement.

00:01:07.215 --> 00:01:09.443
The system did not fail.

00:01:09.443 --> 00:01:13.999
The system worked exactly as designed — for the people it was designed to protect.
